IMPORT prelude

-- Architects Act 1991 (Singapore) -- who may prepare, sign, supply and offer architectural work and call themselves an architect
-- (ss 3, 10-14), the experience routes to registration (s 15(1)-(2AD), (5)), removal and re-application (ss 17B, 17C(2)), the
-- annual practising certificate (ss 18, 19), and the ceilings on licence and disciplinary sanctions (ss 26A(2), 31G, 34).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/AA1991.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 15 of 2026 (in force 1 May 2026) and Act 25 of 2024 (in force 1 October 2025) shown. The arrangement of sections at the
-- head of the deposit is out of step with the body from Part 4 on; this row follows the BODY's numbering (so the Disciplinary
-- Committee's powers are s 31G, as s 17B(2)(c)(ii) cross-refers to them).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the reserved activities and what an
-- architect, a client, a builder or an engineer meets. Not encoded: the Board's constitution and elections (Part 2), the
-- licensing tests for corporations and partnerships in s 20 (beyond noting who may supply), ss 22-25, the complaints and inquiry
-- procedure of Part 7 (beyond the ceilings of s 31G), mutual recognition (s 15A), offences by corporations (ss 35, 35A), and
-- anything left to rules, notifications or exemption orders (ss 15(1)(b), 36, 38).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Architects Act 1991 -- practice`

DECLARE Person HAS
    `acts for the Government as a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a naval or landscape architect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a registered architect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is suspended from practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `needs no practising certificate and acts within registration conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `works under direction or supervision of a qualified architect` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is exempt under section 36 from section 10(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `practises on own account or under an architectural practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an architectural practice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a licensed corporation or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is winding up after its licence ceased` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an allied professional partner of a licensed partnership or LLP` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a builder whose architectural services are provided by a qualified architect or licensed body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a repeat offender` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `3 -- who the Act does not reach`

-- s 3(1): "Nothing in this Act applies to anything done or omitted to be done by the Government or a public officer under the
-- authority of the Government." (2): "This Act does not apply to naval architects and landscape architects."
-- How far s 3(2) reaches (to everything such a person does, or only to naval and landscape work) the text does not say. Read
-- LITERALLY here: the Act's prohibitions do not reach the person at all. That reading is an inference.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act reaches the person` IF
        (NOT `the person`'s `acts for the Government as a public officer`)
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `is a naval or landscape architect`)

§§ `10, 31G(10) -- the qualified architect`

-- Most of Part 3 turns on "a registered architect who has in force a practising certificate". s 31G(10): while a suspension
-- order is in force the person "is not, for the purposes of this Act, to be regarded as having in force a practising
-- certificate".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a practising certificate in force` IF
        `the person`'s `has a practising certificate`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `is suspended from practice`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a qualified architect` IF
        `the person`'s `is a registered architect`
    AND `has a practising certificate in force` `the person`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a registered architect within conditions` IF
        `the person`'s `is a registered architect`
    AND `the person`'s `needs no practising certificate and acts within registration conditions`

§§ `10(1) -- preparing plans`

-- s 10(1): a person must not "draw or prepare any architectural plan, drawing, tracing, design, specification or other
-- document intended to govern the construction, enlargement or alteration of any building" unless (a) a registered architect
-- (i) with a practising certificate or (ii) not required to have one and acting within the conditions of registration; (b)
-- "under the direction or supervision of" such a person; or (c) exempt under s 36.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may prepare building plans` IF
        (NOT `the Act reaches the person` `the person`)
    OR  `is a qualified architect` `the person`
    OR  `is a registered architect within conditions` `the person`
    OR  `the person`'s `works under direction or supervision of a qualified architect`
    OR  `the person`'s `is exempt under section 36 from section 10(1)`

§§ `10(2), (2A) -- signing and submitting`

-- s 10(2): a person must not sign and submit to a building authority or public authority any such plan, or any report or
-- certificate required by law to be signed by an architect, "unless the person is a registered architect who has in force a
-- practising certificate". No supervision exception and no conditional-registration exception here. (2A): "Any document that
-- is signed in contravention of subsection (2) is invalid."
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sign and submit plans` IF
        (NOT `the Act reaches the person` `the person`)
    OR  `is a qualified architect` `the person`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signed submission is invalid` IF
    NOT `may sign and submit plans` `the person`

§§ `10(3), (4) -- the title and holding out`

-- s 10(3)(a), (d): only a registered architect with a practising certificate may use "architect" in a business designation, or
-- "architect" or "Ar." as a title before the name. (b): only such an architect or "an architectural practice" may hold out as
-- authorised to supply architectural services. (4): (3)(b) does not stop a corporation or LLP whose licence has ceased from
-- "carrying on any activity necessary to the winding up".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may use the title architect` IF
        (NOT `the Act reaches the person` `the person`)
    OR  `is a qualified architect` `the person`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may hold out as authorised to supply architectural services` IF
        (NOT `the Act reaches the person` `the person`)
    OR  `is a qualified architect` `the person`
    OR  `the person`'s `is an architectural practice`
    OR  `the person`'s `is winding up after its licence ceased`

§§ `10(5), (5A) -- supplying and offering`

-- s 10(5)(a): a person must not supply architectural services unless (i) a registered architect with a practising certificate
-- "doing so on the person's own account or under, or as an employee of, an architectural practice"; (ii) a registered
-- architect not required to have one, within conditions; or (iii) "a licensed corporation or licensed limited liability
-- partnership". (b): must not OFFER unless a person in (a), or (ii) "an allied professional who is doing so only by reason of
-- being a partner in a licensed partnership or licensed limited liability partnership". (5A): a builder may supply or offer in
-- connection with building works it undertakes "if the architectural services are provided by" a person in (a)(i) or (iii).
-- A licensed PARTNERSHIP is not itself named in (a)(iii); only corporations and LLPs are.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may supply architectural services` IF
        (NOT `the Act reaches the person` `the person`)
    OR  (    `is a qualified architect` `the person`
         AND `the person`'s `practises on own account or under an architectural practice`)
    OR  `is a registered architect within conditions` `the person`
    OR  `the person`'s `is a licensed corporation or limited liability partnership`
    OR  `the person`'s `is a builder whose architectural services are provided by a qualified architect or licensed body`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may offer architectural services` IF
        `may supply architectural services` `the person`
    OR  `the person`'s `is an allied professional partner of a licensed partnership or LLP`

§§ `10(6), (7) -- penalties`

-- s 10(6): contravening (1), (2), (3) or (5): (a) a natural person -- fine up to $5,000; a repeat offender up to $10,000 or
-- 6 months or both; (b) a body corporate -- $5,000; repeat $10,000 (no imprisonment). (7): a repeat offender has at least one
-- earlier conviction under (6), whether before, on or after 6 October 2017.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine under section 10` IS
    IF `the person`'s `is a repeat offender` THEN 10000 ELSE 5000

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum months of imprisonment under section 10` IS
    IF `the person`'s `is a natural person` AND `the person`'s `is a repeat offender` THEN 6 ELSE 0

§§ `11 -- fees`

-- s 11(1): a person "is not entitled to demand, claim or sue for or recover any charge, fee or remuneration" for services
-- supplied or offered if "not authorised by this Act to supply those services". (2): a payer may recover money paid for conduct
-- contravening s 10 "if the person did not know, or have reason to believe, when making payment" that it contravened s 10.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may sue for architectural fees` IF
    `may supply architectural services` `the person`

GIVEN `the conduct contravened section 10` IS A BOOLEAN, `the payer knew or had reason to believe it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payer may recover the payment` IF
    `the conduct contravened section 10` AND (NOT `the payer knew or had reason to believe it`)

§§ `12 -- employing or engaging`

-- s 12(1): a person must not "employ as an architect" anyone but a registered architect with a practising certificate. (1A): a
-- person must not "engage the architectural services of any other person in relation to any building works" unless that person
-- is (a) such an architect or (b) a registered architect not required to have one, acting within conditions. (2): fine up to
-- $2,000; second or subsequent conviction $5,000. The prohibition falls on the CLIENT as well as the practitioner.
GIVEN `the hire` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `employing the hire as an architect is an offence` IF
    NOT `is a qualified architect` `the hire`

GIVEN `the hire` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `engaging the hire for building works is an offence` IF
        (NOT `is a qualified architect` `the hire`)
    AND (NOT `is a registered architect within conditions` `the hire`)

GIVEN `earlier convictions under section 12` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine under section 12` IS
    IF `earlier convictions under section 12` AT LEAST 1 THEN 5000 ELSE 2000

§§ `13, 14 -- minor works and engineers`

-- s 13: nothing prevents an unregistered person "carrying out work in respect of the construction of or repairs to any
-- building" where "plans are not required by any written law to be submitted". s 14: Part 3 does not prevent a professional
-- engineer with a practising certificate (or one under such an engineer's direction), or a licensed engineering practice, from
-- carrying on authorised engineering activity "where to do so does not constitute a substantial part of services within the
-- practice of architecture".
GIVEN `plans must be submitted by law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an unregistered person may do the building work` IF
    NOT `plans must be submitted by law`

GIVEN `is a practising engineer or under one or a licensed engineering practice` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the activity is authorised engineering work` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the activity is a substantial part of architectural services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the engineering exception applies` IF
        `is a practising engineer or under one or a licensed engineering practice`
    AND `the activity is authorised engineering work`
    AND (NOT `the activity is a substantial part of architectural services`)

§ `Architects Act 1991 -- registration`

§§ `15(1), (2), (3) -- the three experience routes`

-- s 15(1): entitled to registration on payment of the fee: (a) a B.Arch from NUS or the University of Singapore, or an M.Arch
-- from NUS or SUTD; (b) another qualification approved by the Minister; (c) a person the Board accepts as "otherwise qualified"
-- who passes prescribed examinations. (2): but only if the person satisfies the Board, after qualifying, of one of:
-- (a) at least 2 years' practical experience "(including practical experience in architectural work in Singapore for a
--     continuous period of at least 12 months)" and a professional practice examination;
-- (b) at least 5 years, "including not less than 2 years" in Singapore with a continuous 12 months "within the 5 years
--     immediately preceding the date of the person's application", and an oral or written examination;
-- (c) at least 10 years, a "commendation or award at any international architectural event" or from a recognised body, and an
--     oral or written examination.
-- (3): the Minister may exempt any person from subsection (2).
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `holds a qualification under section 15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years of practical experience` IS A NUMBER
    `years of practical experience in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
    `longest continuous months in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
    `longest continuous months in Singapore in the last 5 years` IS A NUMBER
    `passed the professional practice examination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `passed a Board oral or written examination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `received an international commendation or award` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempted by the Minister from section 15(2)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets route (a)` IF
        `the applicant`'s `years of practical experience` AT LEAST 2
    AND `the applicant`'s `longest continuous months in Singapore` AT LEAST 12
    AND `the applicant`'s `passed the professional practice examination`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets route (b)` IF
        `the applicant`'s `years of practical experience` AT LEAST 5
    AND `the applicant`'s `years of practical experience in Singapore` AT LEAST 2
    AND `the applicant`'s `longest continuous months in Singapore in the last 5 years` AT LEAST 12
    AND `the applicant`'s `passed a Board oral or written examination`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets route (c)` IF
        `the applicant`'s `years of practical experience` AT LEAST 10
    AND `the applicant`'s `received an international commendation or award`
    AND `the applicant`'s `passed a Board oral or written examination`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to registration` IF
        `the applicant`'s `holds a qualification under section 15(1)`
    AND (    `the applicant`'s `exempted by the Minister from section 15(2)`
         OR  `meets route (a)` `the applicant`
         OR  `meets route (b)` `the applicant`
         OR  `meets route (c)` `the applicant`)

§§ `15(2AA)-(2AD), (6) -- experience before qualifying`

-- Inserted by Act 15 of 2026 from 1 May 2026. (2AA), (2AB): for a person qualifying under (1)(a) or (b) (a degree or an approved
-- qualification), the Board "may only take into account" pre-qualification experience that "(a) commences on or after 1 May
-- 2026; and (b) is acquired in Singapore". (2AC), (2AD): for a person qualifying under (1)(c), it may count experience
-- "whether it commences before, on or after 1 May 2026" and "whether it is acquired in Singapore or elsewhere". It is a
-- discretion ("may"); this rule decides only whether the Board CAN count it. (2AC) counts it only for routes (b) and (c).
DECLARE QualificationRoute IS ONE OF
    `a listed Singapore degree`
    `a Minister-approved qualification`
    `otherwise qualified with Board examinations`

GIVEN `the route` IS A QualificationRoute, `starts on or after 1 May 2026` IS A BOOLEAN, `acquired in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may count the pre-qualification experience` IF
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `otherwise qualified with Board examinations` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `starts on or after 1 May 2026` AND `acquired in Singapore`

§§ `15(5), 17B, 17C -- refusal, removal and return`

-- s 15(5): an applicant refused registration may appeal "within 30 days after being notified" to the General Division of the
-- High Court. s 17B(1): the Board may remove a registered architect who (a) has no address in Singapore for contact, or (b) "has
-- not renewed his or her practising certificate for a continuous period of at least 10 years". (8): a voluntary removal under
-- (5) may not be ordered while disciplinary action is pending, or a complaint not dismissed or an Investigation Committee
-- inquiry concerns the applicant. s 17C(2): the Board may consider a fresh application "after the expiry of at least 3 years"
-- from removal.
GIVEN `days since notice of refusal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a registration appeal is in time` IF
    `days since notice of refusal` AT MOST 30

GIVEN `has a Singapore contact address` IS A BOOLEAN, `continuous years without renewal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may remove the architect for dormancy` IF
        (NOT `has a Singapore contact address`)
    OR  `continuous years without renewal` AT LEAST 10

GIVEN `disciplinary action is pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `an undismissed complaint or inquiry exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `voluntary removal may be ordered` IF
    (NOT `disciplinary action is pending`) AND (NOT `an undismissed complaint or inquiry exists`)

GIVEN `years since removal` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may consider a fresh application` IF
    `years since removal` AT LEAST 3

§ `Architects Act 1991 -- practising certificates`

§§ `18(1), (2), (5), (6) -- the annual deadline`

-- s 18(1): an architect who wants to practise after 31 December must apply "not later than 1 December" for a certificate for the
-- succeeding year. (2): a first application after registration may be made "at any time during the year", for the remainder of
-- that year. (5): a late renewer may still be issued one, with an additional fee: (a) for the succeeding year if applying "during
-- the month of December"; (b) for "the remainder of the year" if applying on or after 1 January. (6): in force until 31 December.
-- A renewal is modelled by whether it is for the FOLLOWING year (on time only up to 1 December) or for the CURRENT year (always
-- late for a renewer: s 18(5)(b), "on or after 1 January of that year").
GIVEN `for the following year` IS A BOOLEAN, `month` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the renewal is on time` IF
        `for the following year`
    AND (    `month` AT MOST 11
         OR  (`month` EQUALS 12 AND `day` AT MOST 1))

GIVEN `is a first application` IS A BOOLEAN, `for the following year` IS A BOOLEAN, `month` IS A NUMBER, `day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an additional fee is payable` IF
    (NOT `is a first application`) AND (NOT `the renewal is on time` `for the following year` `month` `day`)

§§ `18(4), 19 -- refusal and cancellation`

-- s 18(4): the Board MAY refuse a certificate if the applicant (a) is an undischarged bankrupt; (b) has compounded with
-- creditors; (c) does not intend to practise on own account, in partnership or employed by an architectural practice; (d) made a
-- knowingly false declaration; (e) conduct gives reasonable grounds to believe the applicant will not practise lawfully, honestly
-- and with integrity; (f) has not met continuing professional education requirements; (g) the practice name is not approved; (h)
-- the qualification was withdrawn or cancelled; (i) breached Minister's s 15(3) conditions; (j) has not complied with a
-- disciplinary order or registration condition. A mere pending complaint is not among the grounds.
-- s 19(1): the Board may cancel a certificate on any s 18(4) ground "whether or not that ground existed at the time the
-- practising certificate was issued"; (2) only after "an opportunity of being heard".
DECLARE CertificateGround IS ONE OF
    `an undischarged bankrupt`
    `a composition with creditors`
    `no intention to practise in Singapore`
    `a knowingly false declaration`
    `conduct suggesting dishonest practice`
    `continuing professional education not met`
    `practice name not approved`
    `qualification withdrawn`
    `breach of Minister's exemption conditions`
    `an unpaid disciplinary penalty`
    `a complaint not yet heard`
    `a discharged bankruptcy`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A CertificateGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may refuse the certificate` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `a complaint not yet heard` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a discharged bankruptcy` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A CertificateGround, `the architect was given a hearing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may cancel the certificate` IF
    `the Board may refuse the certificate` `the ground` AND `the architect was given a hearing`

§§ `18(8) -- changes of practice name or address`

-- s 18(8): any change in the practice's name or address "must be notified by the registered architect concerned to the Registrar
-- within 2 weeks of the change".
GIVEN `days after the change` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change is notified in time` IF
    `days after the change` AT MOST 14

§ `Architects Act 1991 -- sanctions`

§§ `26A(2), 31G(2), (3), 34 -- ceilings`

-- s 26A(2)(a): where revocation is not warranted, the Board may impose on a licensed corporation, partnership or LLP "a penalty not
-- exceeding $100,000". s 31G(2): a Disciplinary Committee may (a) remove, (b) suspend "for a period of not more than 2 years",
-- (c) impose "a penalty not exceeding $50,000", (d) censure, (e) make any other order; (3) and order costs "not exceeding
-- $10,000". s 34: falsifying a register or procuring registration, a certificate or a licence by false representation: fine up to
-- $5,000 or 6 months or both.
DECLARE DisciplinaryOrder HAS
    `months of suspension` IS A NUMBER
    `penalty` IS A NUMBER
    `costs` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the order` IS A DisciplinaryOrder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order is within section 31G` IF
        `the order`'s `months of suspension` AT MOST 24
    AND `the order`'s `penalty` AT MOST 50000
    AND `the order`'s `costs` AT MOST 10000

GIVEN `penalty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence penalty is within section 26A(2)` IF
    `penalty` AT MOST 100000

GIVEN `fine` IS A NUMBER, `months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sentence is within section 34` IF
    `fine` AT MOST 5000 AND `months of imprisonment` AT MOST 6
